    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "This was said by the Blessed One, said by the Arahant, so I have heard: “Monks, there are these three kinds of unskillful thinking. Which three? Thinking concerned with not wanting to be despised; thinking concerned with gains, offerings, & tribute; thinking concerned with an empathy for others. There are three kinds of unskillful thinking.”"
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Fettered"
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "to not wanting to be despised;"
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "to gains, offerings, respect;"
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "to delight in companions:"
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "you’re far from the ending of fetters."
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "But whoever here,"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "having abandoned"
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "sons,"
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "cattle,"
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "marriage,"
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "intimates:"
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "he’s capable"
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "–a monk like this–"
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "of touching superlative"
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "self-awakening."
    }
  ]
}